1
00:01:09,599 --> 00:01:15,599
Beyond the Walls: In Search of the Celts is a
documentary film directed by David Starkey.

2
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:25,199
Historian Dr Eleanor Barraclough travels through some of Britain's most beautiful landscapes to
reveal the true story of the mysterious British tribes often called the Celts.

3
00:03:28,799 --> 00:03:34,799
Self - Presenter, played by Eleanor Barraclough.

4
00:04:38,399 --> 00:04:44,399
Italy, officially the Italian Republic, is a
country in Southern and Western Europe.

5
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:54,000
It consists of a peninsula that extends into the Mediterranean Sea, with the Alps on its
northern land border, as well as nearly 800 islands, notably Sicily and Sardinia.

6
00:06:57,599 --> 00:07:03,599
Italy shares land borders with France to the west; Switzerland and Austria to the north;
Slovenia to the east; and the two enclaves of Vatican City and San Marino.

7
00:08:07,199 --> 00:08:13,199
It is the tenth-largest country in Europe by area, covering 301,340 km2 (116,350 sq mi), and the
third-most populous member state of the European Union, with nearly 59 million inhabitants.

8
00:09:16,799 --> 00:09:22,799
Italy's capital and largest city is Rome; other major cities include Milan,
Naples, Turin, Palermo, Bologna, Florence, Genoa, and Venice.

9
00:10:26,399 --> 00:10:32,399
The history of Italy goes back to numerous Italic peoples – notably including the ancient Romans, who conquered the
Mediterranean world during the Roman Republic and ruled it for centuries during the Roman Empire.

10
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:42,000
With the spread of Christianity, Rome became the seat
of the Catholic Church and the Papacy.

11
00:12:45,599 --> 00:12:51,599
Barbarian invasions and other factors led to the decline and fall of the Western
Roman Empire between late antiquity and the Early Middle Ages.

12
00:13:55,199 --> 00:14:01,199
By the 11th century, Italian city-states and maritime republics expanded, bringing renewed
prosperity through commerce and laying the groundwork for modern capitalism.

13
00:15:04,799 --> 00:15:10,799
The Italian Renaissance flourished during the 15th and 16th
centuries and spread to the rest of Europe.

14
00:16:14,399 --> 00:16:20,399
Italian explorers discovered new routes to the Far East and the New
World, contributing significantly to the Age of Discovery.

15
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:30,000
After centuries of political and territorial divisions, the Kingdom of Italy was established
in 1861, following wars of independence and the Expedition of the Thousand.

16
00:18:33,599 --> 00:18:39,599
From the late 19th to the early 20th century, Italy industrialised and acquired a colonial empire, while the
south remained largely impoverished, fuelling a large immigrant diaspora to the Americas.

17
00:19:43,199 --> 00:19:49,199
From 1915 to 1918, Italy took part in World War I with
the Entente against the Central Powers.

18
00:20:52,799 --> 00:20:58,799
In 1922, the Italian fascist dictatorship was established.

19
00:22:02,399 --> 00:22:08,399
During World War II, Italy was first part of the Axis until an armistice with the Allied powers (1940–1943), then a co-belligerent of the
Allies during the Italian resistance and liberation of Italy from German occupation and the collaborationist RSI (1943–1945).

20
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:18,000
In 1946, the monarchy was replaced by a republic and
the country made a strong recovery.

21
00:24:21,599 --> 00:24:27,599
A developed country with an advanced economy, Italy has the eighth-largest nominal GDP in the world, the second-largest manufacturing sector in
Europe, and plays a significant role in regional and – to a lesser extent – global economic, military, cultural, and political affairs.

22
00:25:31,199 --> 00:25:37,199
It is a founding and leading member of the European Union, and is part of
numerous other international organisations and forums.

23
00:26:40,799 --> 00:26:46,799
As a cultural superpower, Italy has long been a renowned global centre of art, music, literature, cuisine,
fashion, science and technology, and the source of multiple inventions and discoveries.

24
00:27:50,399 --> 00:27:56,399
It has the highest number of World Heritage Sites (61) and is
the fifth-most visited country in the world.
